quran[12]{c,v,t}:
  27,77,and it is indeed a guidance and a mercy for the believers.
  27,78,"Indeed, your Lord will decide between them by His command. And He is the All-Mighty, the All-Knowing."
  27,79,"So put your trust in Allah. Indeed, you firmly stand on the manifest truth."
  27,80,"Indeed, you cannot make the dead (i.e. the disbelievers) hear, nor can you make the deaf hear the call (of truth) when they turn their backs (and withdraw from you)."
  27,81,Nor can you lead the blind out of their misguidance. You can make none hear (the truth) except those who believe in Our Commandments and submit.
  27,82,"And when the Word (of the final judgement) comes upon them, We shall bring out a beast for them from the earth telling them that the people had no firm faith in Our revelations."
  27,83,"On that day, We shall gather from every community a group of those who rejected Our revelations, and they will be driven in ranks."
  27,84,"When they come (before their Lord), He will say (to them): ‘Did you reject My revelations, while you did not comprehend them in knowledge? What is it that you used to do?’"
  27,85,And the Word (of the final judgement) shall pass against them because of their wrongdoing. So they will not be able to speak.
  27,86,Do they not see We made the night that they may rest in it and the day to provide visibility? There are indeed signs in that for people who believe.
  27,87,"The Day when the trumpet will be blown, all those in the heavens and all those on the earth will be terrified, except whom Allah pleases (to spare). And all will come to Him in utter humility."
  27,88,"You see the mountains, which you suppose are firmly fixed, while they will float away like passing clouds. (This is) the work of Allah, Who has perfected everything. He is indeed well aware of what you do."
